  "closure_boundaries": [
    "manager_editor_actions has real all-ten-target document save/save-and-close/close-without-saving consumers in SFMDocumentActionTarget and registration in SFMClientRegistrations, but this ManagerScreen action-button/member integration exists only on the two oldest targets.",
    "ManagerEditAction, SFMActionButton and their mixed imports must be selected by actual consumers. SFMActionElement/SFMActionElementAudit can be shared pure action-context carriers under OR-consumer membership; this does not require the workspace panel runtime.",
    "Single-line input requires its concrete edit-box/widget/model/accessor and mixin registration closure. No clipboard-history, palette or workspace prerequisite is inferred from interface presence.",
    "Null-safe ManagerScreen sampling is not the 26.1.2 tick-graph renderer change. Existing tick_graph_null_samples support must not be widened.",
    "These twenty ManagerScreen witnesses do not add ClientManagerScreen tooltip or menu-summary bounds behavior. The distinct primary-development ClientManagerScreen owns those existing behaviors and is not authored in this slice.",
    "The DecimalFormat locale TODO is a nonsemantic comment in the historical null-safety delta. It remains grouped with that exact source reconstruction and is not a new functionality claim.",
    "Program-linter source/registration preservation does not prove Mekanism compatibility, generator execution or linter runtime closure."
  ],
